  "interpretation_rules": [
    "A string/model response is data, not executable behavior, unless a recovered receiver interprets it as a command, class, script, process, or typed action.",
    "IXC names are local Java remote identifiers, not hostnames or open ports.",
    "VSB accepts exact daemon-configured operations; the three-string method does not prove arbitrary caller or operation authority.",
    "USB/SD is a proved output sink for Performance Pages; no stock KIM19 consumer edge returns the file to an interpreter.",
    "Every target-dependent edge remains conditional even when its static sender/receiver call graph is proved."
